WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:05.970
On a cold October night in 2003, Shirley Yeats
of Seattle, Washington, was just about to

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.030
get ready for bed when she heard a knock at
the door.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:13.030
She approached the door and asked the person
on the other side to identify themselves.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:18.150
The voice outside responded immediately, it
was a salesman who wanted just a few moments

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.020
of Ms. Yeats' time.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:25.080
This was odd for two reasons - First, it was
almost 10 o'clock at night, much later than

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.350
is usual for door to door salesman.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:31.030
And second, the knock hadn't come from Mrs.
Yeats' front door.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:34.160
It was coming from the door to her bathroom.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.160
Has your home ever been visited by a door-to-door
salesman?

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:41.190
If you were born in the last forty years,
then your answer to that question is probably

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.190
'no'.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:46.880
In the age of online shopping, the idea of
a salesperson going from house to house hawking

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.630
vacuum cleaners or encyclopedia sets feels
like a relic from the past.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:56.510
It's highly unlikely you'd ever see one walking
the streets nowadays, and equally unlikely

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.840
that one would knock on your front door.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.199
However, if you live in Washington State,
you might need to be wary of a certain salesman

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:06.909
who is still doing the rounds.

00:01:06.909 --> 00:01:13.679
SCP - 1879, also known as the Indoor Salesman
and the Door Man, is a phenomenon that manifests

00:01:13.679 --> 00:01:16.560
randomly in homes throughout Washington.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:20.520
Subjects will hear persistent knocking from
the interior doors of their homes, and the

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.180
affected door becomes classified as SCP - 1879
- 1.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:29.719
The knocking doesn't stop until the door is
opened, at which point the subject will be

00:01:29.719 --> 00:01:37.609
greeted by SCP - 1879 - 2, a Caucasian man
of indeterminate age, standing around 170

00:01:37.609 --> 00:01:39.109
cm tall.

00:01:39.109 --> 00:01:43.940
The man will claim to be a salesman, and immediately
try to pitch a bizarre product to the subject

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:45.729
whose home he's just invaded.

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:50.740
The SCP Foundation was first alerted to the
existence of the Indoor Salesman when they

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:54.749
intercepted a 911 call coming from the home
of Mrs. Shirley Yeats.

00:01:54.749 --> 00:02:00.109
She had opened the door to her bathroom in
an attempt to get the salesman to stop knocking,

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:03.489
and once he was in her home, he refused to
leave.

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:08.610
According to Yeats, he kept disappearing in
and out of random doors in her house.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:12.810
Foundation Field Agent Rogers was equipped
with a recording device and sent to investigate

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.330
the case with several other agents.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:20.770
When he arrived at the home, he found Mrs.
Yeats inconsolable.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:25.980
SCP-1879-2 was still rapidly talking at her,
and strangely enough, the product he was holding

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:29.420
and trying to sell to her was a border collie
puppy.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:34.220
As soon as Agent Rogers entered the room,
the man shifted his attention away from Mrs.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.220
Yeats and towards him.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.810
He then started trying to sell the puppy to
Agent Rogers.

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:42.880
Agent Rogers did not want to purchase this
puppy, but he found that the man spoke so

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.180
quickly and urgently, he couldn't get a word
in edgewise.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.820
The man was begging Rogers to take the puppy,
practically shoving it in his face, saying

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:56.200
that he didn’t need any money, and that
the only payment he needed would be 'some

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.380
of your time'.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:01.500
Rogers grew so annoyed at being talked over
and interrupted that he ordered the other

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:04.530
Field Agents to apprehend the Indoor Salesman.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:09.630
They did so, but as soon as the agents walked
him out the front door of the house, he disappeared

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:10.980
without a trace.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:17.190
The agents remained in the area to monitor
the situation, and sure enough, SCP-1879-2

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:21.990
manifested again in Mrs. Yeats' home six hours
later, still trying to trade the puppy for

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.970
no money, just a little of her time.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.690
12 years to be precise.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:32.351
After hours and hours of being worn down by
this supernaturally pushy salesman, Yeats

00:03:32.351 --> 00:03:37.150
relented and agreed to take the puppy… and
immediately disappeared.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:41.180
The Indoor Salesman then disappeared himself
through the closest door before he could be

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.760
apprehended again.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:48.450
At a loss for what to do, the agents administered
Class-A amnestics to Mrs. Yeats' family and

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:49.450
left.

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:54.870
The reason for her disappearance wasn't fully
known until 12 years later in 2015, when she

00:03:54.870 --> 00:04:00.200
reappeared in the same spot she'd disappeared
from, having no concept of how much time had

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.200
passed.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.500
The puppy really had just cost her 12 years
of her life.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:09.850
Stories like that of Shirley Yeats have popped
up all over the state in the years since,

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.830
from Everett to Walla Walla and everywhere
in between.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:19.930
Due to the random nature of SCP-1879 events
and the way that the Indoor Salesman can disappear

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:26.139
instantly in and out of any door in a building,
the SCP Foundation has been unable to capture

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:27.139
him.

00:04:27.139 --> 00:04:31.539
The best they’ve been able to do is monitor
911 calls from across the state, listening

00:04:31.539 --> 00:04:37.659
for key words that might indicate another
SCP-1879 infestation.

00:04:37.659 --> 00:04:43.680
When such an event is reported, the foundation
deploys Mobile Task Force Rho-4, aka “Shoos

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:44.680
Salesmen.”

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:49.180
This task force's entire purpose is to minimize
the amount of harm the Indoor Salesman is

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:53.189
able to cause by intercepting him before he
can make a sale.

00:04:53.189 --> 00:04:58.349
This is a very important task, as evidenced
by the story of Mrs. Yeats, since while the

00:04:58.349 --> 00:05:04.249
products this salesman sells might be innocent,
he doesn't accept payment in any normal currency.

00:05:04.249 --> 00:05:08.590
The prices he asks for his products are always
bizarre, and often deadly.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:13.000
If all someone loses is 12 years of their
life, they could be considered to be getting

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.080
off easy.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:19.469
In one instance, the product being sold was
a single red rose, in exchange for the subject's

00:05:19.469 --> 00:05:20.469
heart.

00:05:20.469 --> 00:05:24.889
Once the deal was sealed, the subject dropped
dead on the spot, with an autopsy revealing

00:05:24.889 --> 00:05:29.789
that his heart and circulatory system vanished
from inside his body.

00:05:29.789 --> 00:05:35.189
In another, the Indoor Salesman offered 220
bananas, and told the subject to simply 'give

00:05:35.189 --> 00:05:36.449
him some sugar'.

00:05:36.449 --> 00:05:40.240
The subject agreed, and all candied goods
in the home disappeared.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:45.319
In a third, the Indoor Salesman was trying
to sell a thermonuclear warhead, the price

00:05:45.319 --> 00:05:47.719
of which was the subject's soul.

00:05:47.719 --> 00:05:51.410
The subject accepted, and at first, nothing
seemed to have happened.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:56.120
The Foundation confiscated the warhead and
placed it into non-anomalous containment.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:00.370
Later that day, the subject went to listen
to some music, only to find that two of her

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:06.370
vinyl records had gone missing - Lady Soul
and Almighty Fire, by world-famous soul singer

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:07.620
Aretha Franklin.

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:13.759
So, even though he's incredibly invasive,
annoying, and his transactions can be deadly,

00:06:13.759 --> 00:06:17.059
the Indoor Salesman still maintains a sense
of humor.

00:06:17.059 --> 00:06:21.389
The fact that the Foundation can't capture
the Indoor Salesman means that a lot of questions

00:06:21.389 --> 00:06:23.860
about him remain unanswered.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:27.729
The biggest by far is why he does what he
does.

00:06:27.729 --> 00:06:34.479
In most SCP-1879 events, the Indoor Salesman
seems frantic and desperate to make a sale.

00:06:34.479 --> 00:06:39.339
Often he will refer to having quotas and deadlines
to meet, which implies some other, unseen

00:06:39.339 --> 00:06:42.199
entity that he has to answer to.

00:06:42.199 --> 00:06:46.999
These questions remain unanswered, because
all attempts to interrogate the Indoor Salesman

00:06:46.999 --> 00:06:48.530
have been unsuccessful.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:53.080
When he manifests in a location, it's impossible
to get him to stray from his sales pitch,

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:57.550
and he disappears as soon as he successfully
sells his wares.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:04.490
However, there was one instance where, after
an SCP-1879 event took place, Foundation agents

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:11.099
were there to witness a rare interaction between
the Indoor Salesman and his mysterious employers.

00:07:11.099 --> 00:07:15.229
Agent Rogers and the rest of the Shoos Salesmen
were called out to a home in Spokane where

00:07:15.229 --> 00:07:19.039
rapid knocking had begun to emanate from the
bedroom door.

00:07:19.039 --> 00:07:23.629
Equipped with recording devices, Rogers was
able to record the voice of the Indoor Salesman

00:07:23.629 --> 00:07:25.220
coming from inside the bedroom.

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:29.809
In the recording, the salesman grumbled to
himself about not being able to meet his quota

00:07:29.809 --> 00:07:34.949
by tomorrow, saying that if he didn't, he'd
be stuck in this world for the next century.

00:07:34.949 --> 00:07:39.099
He started knocking again, yelling through
the door that he knew that he knew they were

00:07:39.099 --> 00:07:40.099
home.

00:07:40.099 --> 00:07:43.590
He kept knocking until he was interrupted
by the sound of a phone ringing.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:48.909
The Indoor Salesman was heard picking it up,
and Rogers managed to record the conversation.

00:07:48.909 --> 00:07:54.319
The person calling was, apparently, the Indoor
Salesman’s boss, who was calling to complain

00:07:54.319 --> 00:07:56.059
about his performance.

00:07:56.059 --> 00:08:00.699
Only one side of the conversation was heard,
but evidently the Indoor Salesman’s boss

00:08:00.699 --> 00:08:05.840
wasn't too happy about receiving two Aretha
Franklin albums as payment instead of an actual

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.080
human soul.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:11.430
The Indoor Salesman apologized for the joke,
then told his boss - “It won't happen again.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:14.360
Please don't hurt it, I'll meet the quota
this time, I swear.”

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:18.729
He hung up, grumbling to himself again, “I
better get to move up to at least Accounting

00:08:18.729 --> 00:08:19.729
this time....

00:08:19.729 --> 00:08:21.439
I've paid my dues and then some.”

00:08:21.439 --> 00:08:25.800
Rogers finally opened the door, to the apparent
disappointment of the Indoor Salesman, who

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:29.819
was hoping to speak with the home’s owner
and was quite annoyed at having another one

00:08:29.819 --> 00:08:32.820
of his sales interrupted by MTF Rho-4.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:37.570
Rogers tried to ask the Indoor Salesman who
he'd just been speaking to on the phone, but

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:40.350
as usual, the Salesman started talking over
him.

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.530
“Now, see here, let's think logically,”
he said.

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:44.710
“You know I'm not gonna tell you anything.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:47.350
I know you're not likely to buy what I'm selling.

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:49.090
So let's just move on to greener pastures.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:52.720
I'm coming up close to a deadline, and I'm
sure you're swamped with making sure good

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:56.180
people don't do their jobs, so I'll just be
on my way and let you do that.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.180
Ciao.”

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:01.190
The Indoor Salesman tried to close the door,
but Agent Rogers blocked it with his arm.

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:06.500
He was tired of this SCP giving him the runaround,
and he was going to keep the Indoor Salesman

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:09.110
here if it was the last thing he did.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:14.050
He demanded the entity stay and be interviewed,
and other members of the task force apprehended

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:17.200
the Salesman, making sure he couldn't leave
the room.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:22.510
The Indoor Salesman, now held in place by
several armed men, seemed to finally relent.

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:25.340
He told Rogers - “I'm busy, so I'll tell
you what.

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:28.480
I'm going to give you something, no money
out of your pocket, and we'll call it even.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:29.480
Sound good?”

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:33.790
Rogers, just wanting to get this whole thing
over with, agreed to these terms.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:39.160
Three seconds later, every agent on the scene
was dead, and the Indoor Salesman was able

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:43.970
to straighten his tie, pick up his briefcase
and walk through the door to the bathroom.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:49.620
When the bodies of Agent Rogers and the rest
of MTF Rho-4 were examined by Foundation scientists,

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:54.950
the cause of death was found to be, in every
case, thousands of coins suddenly appearing

00:09:54.950 --> 00:10:00.900
in not only their pockets, but also inside
their stomachs, lungs, and even under their

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:01.900
skin.

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:05.970
Later that day, the Indoor Salesman was reported
at a home in the same neighborhood.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:11.980
He was seen trying to sell the house's owner
- 80-year-old retiree Alan Johnson - a Glock-18

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:14.930
pistol in exchange for 'his attention.’

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:19.930
As he had done so many times before, the Indoor
Salesman disappeared through another door

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:25.250
before the Foundation were able to reach the
scene, and when the SCP arrived, they found

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:31.370
Mr. Johnson, still alive but now missing his
prefrontal cortex - the part of the brain

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:33.200
that controls attention.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:40.100
It's likely that, because of the nature of
the entity, SCP-1879 might be entirely impossible

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:41.180
to contain.

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:45.280
The Foundation might never find out anything
more than what they already know about the

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:50.410
Indoor Salesman, the way he's able to manifest
behind closed doors, or the reason he has

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:55.600
to keep filling quotas for an unseen boss
who, apparently, doesn't have a very good

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:57.020
sense of humor.

00:10:57.020 --> 00:11:02.850
So, if you're ever in Washington state, be
careful who you open your doors to, especially

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:07.810
if the knocking you hear is coming from inside
your house.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:10.870
But now, if we could have just a few moments
of your time, we’ve got something special

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:11.870
for you.

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:15.060
It’s SCP-001, Which is the Real 001!

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:18.240
This is a thirty for one deal that you can’t
pass up so go watch now!

